  "worked_solution": "The eigenvector $v=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$ corresponds to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =1.$ So, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Av & =1v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we have the following picture:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14121671/assets/221b02b2df0cd292a41593f52b96be20c0ed20c1b1ccad080157f4729d871f0c.png)",
